# Cloud sync with Supabase (optional)
#
# Supabase dashboard -> your project -> Connect -> Framework -> React (Vite).
# Copy the project URL and the publishable key (sb_publishable_..., or the
# legacy anon key). Both are safe to ship in the app: row-level security on
# public.dayflow_records keeps each account's rows private.
# NEVER use the service_role / secret key here.
#
# Then run supabase/migrations/20261114120000_dayflow_records.sql once in the
# Supabase SQL editor. Setting these makes sign-in REQUIRED; leave them empty
# to build a local-only app with no login.
#
# Some Indian networks block *.supabase.co, so the URL can be the site's own
# proxy (vercel.json), e.g. https://dayflow-one-blue.vercel.app/supabase.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=""
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# Bank spends from messaging-app notifications. Leave off for Play builds: the
# native notification listener it needs is not on main and only exists on the
# feature/bank-sms-notifications branch (sideload / personal builds only).
VITE_ENABLE_BANK_SMS="false"
